# sgo.build — plan 0038's call-in leg. Can an ObjC method's BODY be Sgola?
# The spike registers a callback (`go.callback`, ruled sgola 29536af, not yet
# landed), installs its address as an IMP on a runtime-synthesized class, and
# msgSends the method — control enters Sgola from the ObjC runtime. Like the
# call-out spike, no Go code of ours sits in the chain: `go-pkgs/puredep` is
# the same no-functions dependency-plumbing module, and `purego` is reached
# through a facade in the app's own sources.
mode app
emitname callback-spike
binname callback-spike
gomod callbackspike
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/puredep ../go-pkgs/puredep
